ucspi-tcp
=========

ucspi-tcp 0.88, by D. J. Bernstein, from https://cr.yp.to/ucspi-tcp.html
(https://cr.yp.to/ucspi-tcp/ucspi-tcp-0.88.tar.gz, SHA-256
4a0615cab74886f5b4f7e8fd32933a07b955536a3476d74ea087a3ea66a23e9c). Its
author placed it in the public domain on 2007-12-28
(https://cr.yp.to/distributors.html).

Only what Belka builds is here: tcpserver, tcprules, tcprulescheck and
tcpclient, with the library sources they are linked from, and README,
VERSION and CHANGES. The other programs (recordio, argv0, the mconnect,
http@ and rblsmtpd ones, addcr and the rest) and ucspi-tcp's own build
and install are not. Belka builds the programs without its Makefile
(see mk/userland.mk), choosing for each system header the variant that
fits Belka, as for djbdns:

    uint32.h1 -> uint32.h       uint32 is an unsigned int
    uint64.h1 -> uint64.h       uint64 is an unsigned long long
    iopause.h2 -> iopause.h     iopause by poll(2)
    select.h2 -> select.h
    hasshsgr.h1 -> hasshsgr.h   setgroups(2) takes gid_t, not short
    hassgact.h2 -> hassgact.h   sigaction(2)
    hassgprm.h2 -> hassgprm.h   sigprocmask(2)
    haswaitp.h2 -> haswaitp.h   waitpid(2)

The sources are C89, built as such, with <unistd.h>, <arpa/inet.h> and
<stdio.h> included ahead of each.

Changed for Belka:

    error.h         <errno.h> for errno, not "extern int errno" (errno
                    is thread-local in mlibc)
    prot.c          <grp.h> and <unistd.h>, for setgroups and setgid
    readwrite.h     <unistd.h> for read and write, not its own externs
    alloc.c         <stdlib.h> for malloc and free, not its own externs
    socket.h        prototypes for socket_tcpnodelay and
                    socket_ipoptionskill
    tcprules.c      "open.h" and "scan.h", for the calls it makes
    tcprulescheck.c "open.h"

tcpserver is Belka's inetd: /etc/rc.d/inetd starts one for each service
of /etc/inetd.conf, with its rules, if it has any, from
/etc/inetd/<name>.rules made into a cdb by tcprules.
